# Persisted run output is large and regenerable -- a single 12-hour run is ~86MB
# of frames.jsonl, and `git add -A` while a run is still writing will happily
# sweep it in (#760 batch 4 did exactly that, twice). Runs are referenced by id
# in the #760 write-ups and reproduced with `serve_penn.py --re-run <RUN_ID>`,
# so the directory itself does not belong in the history.
#
# This does NOT untrack the handful of small run dirs already committed on main
# -- .gitignore has no effect on tracked files. To commit a new one deliberately,
# `git add -f`.
run-*/
